  📗
    The answer to a probe: 200 and {"status":"ok"} when the server is not
    stopping and every check passes, with the checks listed when there are
    any; 503 and "failing" when one does not; 503 and "stopping", with no
    check asked, once a stop was asked for. Never to be cached.

    One probe at a time asks the checks. A probe that finds another still
    asking does not wait and does not ask too: for a second it answers with
    what the checks last said, and after that with a 503 that names the
    check that has not come back as "slow". So a check that hangs holds one
    worker and makes the server look unwell, which it is, where it would
    otherwise take a worker with every probe until there were none.
